END OF THE LINE (MOVING MEMORY)

A train that never stopped — even after it stopped being yours
FORMAT (LOCKED)

Duration: 25 seconds
Aspect Ratio: 9:16 (vertical)
FPS: 48
Color: Black & white, high-latitude contrast, soft halation
Grain: Fine analog film grain (constant, non-distracting)

CORE RULES

❌ NO ESTABLISHING SHOTS
❌ NO PEOPLE (NO silhouettes, NO reflections of bodies)
❌ NO STATIC FRAMES

✅ Train is already moving at 0.0s
✅ Camera always in motion (micro-drift minimum)
✅ Environment moves subtly even when “still”
✅ Memory ≠ reality (gentle temporal bleed only)

WORLD LOGIC (LOCKED)
The train has been running long before we arrive
The route exists only as remembered motion
Infrastructure continues out of familiarity, not duty
Time does not fracture — it softens
Snow does not erase violently — it covers gently
Nothing fails. Nothing alarms. Things are simply no longer held

CAMERA LANGUAGE
POV-adjacent, remembered rather than witnessed
Slight handheld inertia, like following something you won’t catch
Focus breathes slowly, never snaps
Motion is forward and continuous, no hesitation
Camera may choose to stop following — the train never does

SCENE BREAKDOWN (ALL SHOTS < 2.0s)
0.0 – 2.0s
Train already in motion.
Camera glides alongside the tracks, matching speed.

Snow slides smoothly past.
No vibration, no threat.

Audio: low electrical hum + far wind

2.0 – 4.0s
Camera drifts closer to the rear of the train.
Metal surface carries faint reflections of city lights — blurred, warm.

Reflections feel remembered, not incorrect.

4.0 – 6.0s
Window reflection reveals an older skyline for a moment.
Not a glitch — a lingering thought.

The image fades naturally back to the present.

Audio: distant PA crackle, unintelligible syllables

6.0 – 8.0s
Tracks stretch forward, perfectly aligned.
Snow gathers softly between rails.

8.0 – 10.0s

Interior glimpse through window:
Empty seats, warm overhead light.

This is not abandonment —
this is after everyone went home.

10.0 – 12.0s

Camera eases slightly behind the train.
The train continues without adjusting to us.

12.0 – 14.0s

Snow thickens in the air, muffling sound.
Movement slows perceptually, not physically.

14.0 – 16.0s

Camera begins to lose pace.
The train gains distance — calmly, unapologetically.

PA system activates softly:

“End of the Line—”
Cut before destination is spoken

16.0 – 18.0s

City skyline recedes into haze.
No era change. No flicker.

Just distance.

18.0 – 20.0s

Camera lifts slightly, no longer chasing.
The train keeps moving forward, uninterrupted.

This is the release moment.

20.0 – 23.0s

Train fades into snowfall and depth.
Tracks remain, but no urgency to follow them.

23.0 – 25.0s

Camera continues drifting forward alone.
Final POV drift into white snowfield
Wind fades
Electrical hum cuts abruptly
END ON SILENCE

[SOUND DESIGN]

SFX AND FX:
Emphasis on:
Electrical hum
Wind without direction
PA artifacts (memory fragments)
Silence is treated as an event

